 ## Operating characteristics
 
-*   **Time Complexity:** Depends on the number of active cells and vertices. Subdivision is $O(1)$ per cell but triggers recursive updates [S1]. Simplification is $O(N)$ where $N$ is the total number of cells, but runs only at idle [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Higher than fixed-resolution grids for sparse details due to hierarchy overhead, but lower than uniform high-resolution grids. Vertex sharing reduces memory usage for adjacent cells [S1].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Not given in the sources.
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Not given in the sources.
 *   **Strengths:** Interactive visual feedback (updating coarse levels first), smooth blending ($C^1$ continuity), local detail capture [S1].
 *   **Limitations:** Simplification is drastic (destroys non-surface cells), requires explicit caching for subdivision correctness, fixed subdivision factor ($n=4$) may not be optimal for all shapes [S1].
